ed2.png)\n\nWhat is the surface area of the box shown above knowing that  it is $4\\,\\text{m}$ long, $1\\,\\text{m}$ wide, and $1\\,\\text{m}$ tall?" :question/worked-solution "First, let's consider the net of our box.\n\n \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13986308/assets/c35bb0f7b049baa569a06532b516436afaf310e28870cfbd4790467d36e54809.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n \n\nFrom the diagram, we have squares and rectangles.\n\nThe rectangles are $4\\,\\text{m}$ long and $1\\,\\text{m}$ high. So, the area of one rectangle is:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area of the rectangle}=4\\times 1=4\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe squares has the side equal to $1\\,\\text{m}.$ Hence, the area of one square is:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area of the square}=1\\times 1=1\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the surface area of the box consists of $4$ rectangles and $2$ squares. \n\nTherefore, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =4\\times (\\text{Area of the rectangle})+2\\times (\\text{Area of the square}) \\\\  & =4\\times 4+2\\times 1 \\\\  & =16+2 \\\\  & =18\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-62107/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "947eb2bb-0443-5740-9d45-847c70877270"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-62107"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-93344/selection/cf7484ebfb4d60d7a79e86dca66faabade841d93852f24bb33d7479ed34e1390" :answer/id #uuid "8521792f-d538-5df8-8a2a-d51bcf60cb83" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "36\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93344/selection/3a1a28677265bc274325092470f13b4c0d26d91d559585517ba30a2b11f48cdf" :answer/id #uuid "a78474d8-faff-5377-8744-aa009fc440d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "32\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93344/selection/9c8e5a985307c0380c82b845424311b3f55c05ea8ac25dbe539081353962c8a8" :answer/id #uuid "0bac7c75-2ff4-57e9-bf96-c76c797c56de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "48\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93344/selection/99d864595b004f601ef09eb43d728033401f153bcf4b49905b6c5ee5d0e81a87" :answer/id #uuid "9bc4a283-631b-542b-a40a-8549e8af4be5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "54\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93344/selection/a723400243b9dabe754c173be177a75c3ed6bb9bccad6f731e90e8bf4528f73b" :answer/id #uuid "8e84c650-79aa-5dcc-84a5-436aaf55157c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "28\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93344/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8e4d2e37-fa03-57d9-bc52-91125e82bd7c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-93344/selection/cf7484ebfb4d60d7a79e86dca66faabade841d93852f24bb33d7479ed34e1390" :answer-field/choices ["q-93344/selection/cf7484ebfb4d60d7a79e86dca66faabade841d93852f24bb33d7479ed34e1390" "q-93344/selection/3a1a28677265bc274325092470f13b4c0d26d91d559585517ba30a2b11f48cdf" "q-93344/selection/9c8e5a985307c0380c82b845424311b3f55c05ea8ac25dbe539081353962c8a8" "q-93344/selection/99d864595b004f601ef09eb43d728033401f153bcf4b49905b6c5ee5d0e81a87" "q-93344/selection/a723400243b9dabe754c173be177a75c3ed6bb9bccad6f731e90e8bf4528f73b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-93344" :question/id #uuid "a74df61c-37fc-529e-af44-1edb9c8a16fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-93344" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13986308/assets/76e1fb6d652758a0e20877d7cacbd1172a0073d2ada557d1761ab6e59aab06d9.png)\n\nA gardening company is making metal spikes from the net shown above. What is the total surface area of the spike?" :question/worked-solution "The net shown corresponds to a rectangular pyramid. The surface area of our pyramid consists of $1$ square (base) and $4$ triangles (side faces). \n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =1\\times (\\text{Area of the base})+4\\times (\\text{Area of the side}) \\\\  & =1\\times 12+4\\times 6 \\\\  & =12+24 \\\\  & =36\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-93344/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1233be4b-7634-5882-9ae5-3200a9da71d8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-93344"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-120078/selection/87e8149a24f21b5d8d950d9d19d6be2700ce9404174ee9c732437f80d9f9022a" :answer/id #uuid "fe8b9ab2-e01a-5b59-93c4-4bb629b755bd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "336\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120078/selection/ab3acd9f39fd17f6567843399627a758466a2fd125ee10c8e66465f03c726ac8" :answer/id #uuid "be068561-3b93-58f9-a599-4f8d05798c25" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "324\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120078/selection/ac3d2ff722fe7936b4346d5424eeb9a9e63b824d5ce4b967c00c5e5b2057aba0" :answer/id #uuid "7e554324-d412-58e4-9b70-5dff1e735b0d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "354\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120078/selection/bee9694185646b05df1c291ae782b4fef6a87689e303621930bfc034335222f6" :answer/id #uuid "c738d2b8-ba7f-5c99-8724-113ff5888206" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "348\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120078/selection/efc7008b72ac8220579da5b9fcce39f4defe584abce4e0e73ade161ebd44ac6d" :answer/id #uuid "1ebb305a-5310-5baf-b0cf-78711d9eb5ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "316\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120078/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a28095ac-adf3-50ac-b7cb-8f1aa95fde21" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-120078/selection/ab3acd9f39fd17f6567843399627a758466a2fd125ee10c8e66465f03c726ac8" :answer-field/choices ["q-120078/selection/87e8149a24f21b5d8d950d9d19d6be2700ce9404174ee9c732437f80d9f9022a" "q-120078/selection/ab3acd9f39fd17f6567843399627a758466a2fd125ee10c8e66465f03c726ac8" "q-120078/selection/ac3d2ff722fe7936b4346d5424eeb9a9e63b824d5ce4b967c00c5e5b2057aba0" "q-120078/selection/bee9694185646b05df1c291ae782b4fef6a87689e303621930bfc034335222f6" "q-120078/selection/efc7008b72ac8220579da5b9fcce39f4defe584abce4e0e73ade161ebd44ac6d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-120078" :question/id #uuid "2c2645ff-704d-5d0e-a816-127a2f8fd501" :question/math-academy-id "q-120078" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13986308/assets/8b618c8e43dbe898a6e1c481f4f887a50bc2e8c658368876be11ec5ea269a50c.png)\n\nA company produces a chocolate bar that comes in an triangular-prism-shaped box. In the figure, the areas of some of the faces are displayed in a net of the prism. What is the total surface area of the box?" :question/worked-solution "The surface area of our prism consists of $2$ triangles (base and top) and $3$ rectangles (central and side faces). \n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =2\\times (\\text{Area of the base})+2\\times (\\text{Area of the side faces}) \\\\  & +1\\times (\\text{Area of the central face}) \\\\  & =2\\times 36+2\\times 72+108 \\\\  & =72+144+108 \\\\  & =324\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-120078/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1233be4b-7634-5882-9ae5-3200a9da71d8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-120078"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-120095/selection/4e6d7d9f20f14023df71f320c786c67147e345eeb5660d3b93b237bc645313b1" :answer/id #uuid "0a815c2f-4fb2-5ca0-8b25-3b0628a86930" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,400\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :