hacademy/question-capture/13986308/assets/a7f100b99cdd9ff4f19209be8df1ae01d4cf1254d67f985cd6de41aefbf51e31.png)\n\nJill unfolds a cardboard box and obtains a net shown above. What is the total surface area of the box?" :question/worked-solution "The net shown corresponds to a rectangular prism. The surface area of our prism consists of $2$ squares (base and top) and $4$ rectangles (side faces). \n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =2\\times (\\text{Area of the base})+4\\times (\\text{Area of the side}) \\\\  & =2\\times 360+4\\times 420 \\\\  & =720+1\\,680 \\\\  & =2\\,400\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-120095/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1233be4b-7634-5882-9ae5-3200a9da71d8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-120095"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
